'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... test_hub75_cube_fold.spin2
''   Purpose.... Cube fold self-test: pushes fixed face coordinates through the cube fold and checks each against a hand-computed answer
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- Copyright (c) 2024 Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 08 Oct 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ Description:

   Runs on the P2 with no panels attached: it never starts the display, so no cog starts and no
   pin is driven, and it needs no edit to isp_hub75_hwPanelConfig.spin2 (it does not even use
   it). It folds a reference net with isp_hub75_cube.foldNet() into the tables of adapter 1
   (chain index 0), then pushes a fixed list of face coordinates through the fold and compares
   each result with an answer computed by hand and written below. It prints one PASS or FAIL
   line per case, a total, then END_SESSION.

   The reference cube (face size 8), as the flat picture of its net (P = panel position):

              col 0     col 1     col 2     col 3
     row 0      --     [C5 P0]      --        --        FRONT  (its up points <)
     row 1   [C0 P1]   [C1 P2]   [C2 P3]   [C3 P4]      TOP (v)  LEFT (<)  BOTTOM (^)  RIGHT (>)
     row 2      --        --     [C4 P5]      --        BACK   (v)

   Top is C0 and Front is C5; the four faces' turns in their cells are all different, so every
   quarter turn from face to panel is exercised.

   Groups (the labels match the case tables of the task #79 design):
     N, X - net recognition: the 11 cube nets fold (0 problems), four non-nets and a front
            opposite the top are each rejected (1 problem); the reference net folds last
     G    - on a face, no fold: face coordinates to panel coordinates on every face
     E    - all 24 directed edge crossings
     V    - the five edges the flat picture shows: the last pixel on a face and the first one
            past its edge are neighbours on the display
     A-F  - runs over two and three faces, and full rings
     K    - every corner gap (four per face, so each of the 8 cube corners three times)
     c, j - a circle of radius 3 centred on the corner pixel FRONT (0,0): three quarter-circles
            (FRONT, TOP, LEFT), three points in the corner gap, and the joins at all three edges
     h    - the home of an object: the face that holds its centre, and the transform into it
     I    - faces that are not cube faces
     b, o, s, q, t - the face-centric drawing entries of task #80: a box crossing an edge (b), a
            circle crossing an edge (o), a circle straddling a corner off-centre (s), a circle
            straddling a corner on the face that holds its centre (q), and text crossing an
            edge (t). Each case is one pixel that the primitive draws (a probe) and the display
            pixel it must land on. The case runs the two cube calls the display uses to draw
            every face primitive: homeOnFaceOfExtent() on the rectangle the object spans, then
            homeFoldToDisplay() on the probe. The display code that chooses the rectangle (a
            line's ends, a box's corners, a text run, a circle's centre) and enumerates the
            pixels (Bresenham, the glyph bitmap) is not in this test: the probes are pixels
            those enumerations produce, picked by hand, and the rig confirms the rest.
}

CON ' ---- Timing ----

    CLK_FREQ = 335_000_000                                        ' system freq as a constant
    _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ                                           ' set system clock

CON ' ---- Debug Pins ----

    DEBUG_COGS = %11111111
    DEBUG_BAUD = 2_000_000

CON ' ---- Reference Cube ----

    TEST_CHAIN          = 0                                       ' fold into adapter 1's tables; nothing configures them here
    FACE_SIZE           = 8                                       ' pixel rows (and columns) of one face of the reference cube
    NET_CELLS           = 6                                       ' cells (and cable positions) in a net

    ' foldNet() results expected by group N
    NET_FOLDS           = 0                                       ' no problems: the cube's tables are built
    NET_REJECTED        = 1                                       ' one problem reported

    ' two display pixels are neighbours when |row step| + |column step| is this
    DISPLAY_NEIGHBOURS  = 1

CON ' ---- Case Records ----

    ' a net case (group N):
    '  NET_LABEL    - label letter
    '  NET_NUMBER   - label number
    '  NET_ROWS     - NET_CELLS LONGs: grid row of each cable position's cell
    '  NET_COLUMNS  - NET_CELLS LONGs: grid column of each cable position's cell
    '  NET_TOP      - cable position of the top face
    '  NET_FRONT    - cable position of the front face
    '  NET_EXPECTED - problems foldNet() should report
    #0, NET_LABEL, NET_NUMBER, NET_ROWS
    NET_COLUMNS         = NET_ROWS + NET_CELLS
    #NET_COLUMNS + NET_CELLS, NET_TOP, NET_FRONT, NET_EXPECTED, NET_CASE_LONGS

    ' a fold case (groups G, E, A-F, K, c, j, I):
    '  FOLD_LABEL .. FOLD_NUMBER          - label letter and number
    '  FOLD_FACE, FOLD_ROW, FOLD_COL       - the face coordinates pushed through the fold
    '  FOLD_EXP_FACE .. FOLD_EXP_COL       - the face and face coordinates they land on
    '  FOLD_EXP_PANEL .. FOLD_EXP_PANEL_COL - the panel position and panel coordinates they land on
    #0, FOLD_LABEL, FOLD_NUMBER, FOLD_FACE, FOLD_ROW, FOLD_COL, FOLD_EXP_FACE, FOLD_EXP_ROW, FOLD_EXP_COL, ...
        FOLD_EXP_PANEL, FOLD_EXP_PANEL_ROW, FOLD_EXP_PANEL_COL, FOLD_CASE_LONGS

    ' a seam pair (group V): the last pixel on a face (A) and the first one past its edge (B):
    '  PAIR_LABEL .. PAIR_NUMBER           - label letter and number
    '  PAIR_FACE_A, PAIR_ROW_A, PAIR_COL_A - the last pixel on the face: face and face coordinates
    '  PAIR_FACE_B, PAIR_ROW_B, PAIR_COL_B - the first pixel past its edge: face and face coordinates
    '  PAIR_CASE_LONGS                     - longs in one record
    #0, PAIR_LABEL, PAIR_NUMBER, PAIR_FACE_A, PAIR_ROW_A, PAIR_COL_A, PAIR_FACE_B, PAIR_ROW_B, PAIR_COL_B, PAIR_CASE_LONGS

    ' a home case (group h): an object's centre, and its expected home face and transform:
    '  HOME_LABEL .. HOME_NUMBER           - label letter and number
    '  HOME_FACE, HOME_ROW, HOME_COL       - the object's centre: face and face coordinates
    '  HOME_EXP_FACE                       - the face the object must be homed on
    '  HOME_EXP_TURN                       - the quarter turns into the home frame
    '  HOME_EXP_ADD_ROW, HOME_EXP_ADD_COL  - the row and column added after the turn
    '  HOME_CASE_LONGS                     - longs in one record
    #0, HOME_LABEL, HOME_NUMBER, HOME_FACE, HOME_ROW, HOME_COL, HOME_EXP_FACE, HOME_EXP_TURN, HOME_EXP_ADD_ROW, HOME_EXP_ADD_COL, HOME_CASE_LONGS

    ' an extent case (groups b, o, s, q, t): an object that spans a rectangle of pixels on a face,
    ' one probe pixel of it, and where the probe must land:
    '  EXT_LABEL .. EXT_NUMBER             - label letter and number
    '  EXT_FACE                            - the face the object's coordinates are on
    '  EXT_FIRST_ROW .. EXT_LAST_COL       - the rectangle the object spans (first and last row and column)
    '  EXT_PROBE_ROW, EXT_PROBE_COL        - one pixel of the object, in the same coordinates
    '  EXT_EXP_HOME                        - the face that must hold the rectangle's midpoint
    '  EXT_EXP_ROW, EXT_EXP_COL            - the display row and column the probe must land on, or NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL
    #0, EXT_LABEL, EXT_NUMBER, EXT_FACE, EXT_FIRST_ROW, EXT_FIRST_COL, EXT_LAST_ROW, EXT_LAST_COL, ...
        EXT_PROBE_ROW, EXT_PROBE_COL, EXT_EXP_HOME, EXT_EXP_ROW, EXT_EXP_COL, EXT_CASE_LONGS

CON ' ---- Printed Lines ----

    LINE_BYTES          = 160                                     ' the longest line is a fold FAIL line, about 110 characters
    ONES_PLACE          = 1

OBJ

    cube        : "isp_hub75_cube"
    hwEnum      : "isp_hub75_hwEnums"

DAT ' ---- the reference net and its hand-computed panel origins ----

' panel position of each cable position C0 .. C5 (reading order over the flat picture)
refCablePositions   BYTE    1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 0

' display coordinates of each panel's top-left pixel, by panel position P0 .. P5 (hand table)
panelOriginRows     LONG    0, 8, 8, 8, 8, 16
panelOriginColumns  LONG    8, 0, 8, 16, 24, 16

DAT ' ---- group N: net recognition ----

' label, number, cell rows C0..C5, cell columns C0..C5, top, front, expected problems
netCases
    LONG    "N",  1,   1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2,   0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 0,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 1-4-1, flaps (0,0) (2,0)
    LONG    "N",  2,   1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2,   0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 1,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 1-4-1, flaps (0,0) (2,1)
    LONG    "N",  3,   1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2,   0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 2,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 1-4-1, flaps (0,0) (2,2)
    LONG    "N",  4,   1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2,   0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 3,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 1-4-1, flaps (0,0) (2,3)
    LONG    "N",  5,   1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2,   0, 1, 2, 3, 1, 1,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 1-4-1, flaps (0,1) (2,1)
    LONG    "N",  6,   1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 2,   0, 1, 2, 3, 1, 2,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 1-4-1, flaps (0,1) (2,2)
    LONG    "N",  7,   1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 2,   1, 2, 3, 1, 0, 1,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 2-3-1, bottom (2,1)
    LONG    "N",  8,   1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 2,   1, 2, 3, 1, 0, 2,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 2-3-1, bottom (2,2)
    LONG    "N",  9,   1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 2,   1, 2, 3, 1, 0, 3,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 2-3-1, bottom (2,3)
    LONG    "N", 10,   0, 0, 1, 1, 2, 2,   0, 1, 1, 2, 2, 3,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 2-2-2
    LONG    "N", 11,   0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1,   0, 1, 2, 2, 3, 4,   0, 1, NET_FOLDS       ' 3-3
    ' each non-net prints its "do not fold into a cube" message, then reports 1 problem
    LONG    "X",  1,   1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0,   0, 1, 2, 3, 2, 0,   0, 1, NET_REJECTED    ' two flaps above: C4 and C5 both fold to +Z
    LONG    "X",  2,   0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1,   0, 1, 2, 0, 1, 2,   0, 1, NET_REJECTED    ' 2 x 3: C3 and C4 both fold to -Z
    LONG    "X",  3,   1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0,   0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 0,   0, 1, NET_REJECTED    ' a row of 5 and 1: C0 and C4 both face the viewer
    LONG    "X",  4,   0, 1, 2, 3, 3, 3,   0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 2,   0, 1, NET_REJECTED    ' an L of 4 and 2: C1 and C5 both fold to -Z
    ' the reference net with the front opposite the top prints its message, then reports 1 problem
    LONG    "N", 12,   0, 0, 0, 0, 1, -1,  0, 1, 2, 3, 2, 1,   0, 2, NET_REJECTED    ' front C2 is opposite top C0
    ' the reference net runs last, so the fold cases below read its tables
    LONG    "N", 13,   0, 0, 0, 0, 1, -1,  0, 1, 2, 3, 2, 1,   0, 5, NET_FOLDS       ' the reference cube: top C0, front C5
netCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- group G: on a face, no fold ----

' label, number, face, row, column -> face, row, column, panel position, panel row, panel column
onFaceCases
    LONG    "G", 1, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    1, 2,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    1, 2,  1, 6, 5
    LONG    "G", 2, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 1, 2,  hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 1, 2,  3, 1, 2
    LONG    "G", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  1, 2,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  1, 2,  0, 5, 1
    LONG    "G", 4, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   1, 2,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   1, 2,  5, 6, 5
    LONG    "G", 5, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   1, 2,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   1, 2,  2, 5, 1
    LONG    "G", 6, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  1, 2,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  1, 2,  4, 2, 6
    LONG    "G", 7, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  0, 0,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  0, 0,  0, 7, 0
    LONG    "G", 8, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  7, 7,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  7, 7,  0, 0, 7
onFaceCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- group E: all 24 directed edge crossings ----

' label, number, face, row, column -> face, row, column, panel position, panel row, panel column
edgeCases
    LONG    "E",  1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -2,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    6, 3,  1, 1, 4     ' FRONT.N
    LONG    "E",  2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1, 11,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  1, 3,  4, 3, 6     ' FRONT.E
    LONG    "E",  3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  11,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 3, 2,  3, 3, 2     ' FRONT.S
    LONG    "E",  4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   4, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   4, 6,  2, 1, 4     ' FRONT.W
    LONG    "E",  5, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   -2,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    1, 4,  1, 6, 3     ' BACK.N
    LONG    "E",  6, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,    1, 11,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   1, 3,  2, 4, 1     ' BACK.E
    LONG    "E",  7, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   11,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 4, 5,  3, 4, 5     ' BACK.S
    LONG    "E",  8, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,    4, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  4, 6,  4, 6, 3     ' BACK.W
    LONG    "E",  9, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   -2,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    3, 1,  1, 4, 6     ' LEFT.N
    LONG    "E", 10, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,    1, 11,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  1, 3,  0, 4, 1     ' LEFT.E
    LONG    "E", 11, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   11,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 5, 3,  3, 5, 3     ' LEFT.S
    LONG    "E", 12, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,    4, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   4, 6,  5, 3, 1     ' LEFT.W
    LONG    "E", 13, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  -2,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    4, 6,  1, 3, 1     ' RIGHT.N
    LONG    "E", 14, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,   1, 11,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   1, 3,  5, 6, 4     ' RIGHT.E
    LONG    "E", 15, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  11,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 2, 4,  3, 2, 4     ' RIGHT.S
    LONG    "E", 16, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,   4, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  4, 6,  0, 1, 4     ' RIGHT.W
    LONG    "E", 17, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    -2,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   1, 4,  5, 6, 3     ' TOP.N
    LONG    "E", 18, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,     1, 11,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  3, 6,  4, 6, 4     ' TOP.E
    LONG    "E", 19, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    11,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  3, 2,  0, 5, 3     ' TOP.S
    LONG    "E", 20, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,     4, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   1, 4,  2, 3, 1     ' TOP.W
    LONG    "E", 21, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, -2,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  6, 3,  0, 4, 6     ' BOTTOM.N
    LONG    "E", 22, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,  1, 11,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  4, 1,  4, 1, 3     ' BOTTOM.E
    LONG    "E", 23, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 11,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   4, 5,  5, 3, 2     ' BOTTOM.S
    LONG    "E", 24, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,  4, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   6, 3,  2, 4, 6     ' BOTTOM.W
edgeCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- group V: the five edges the flat picture shows ----

' label, number, last pixel on a face (face, row, column), first pixel past its edge (face, row, column)
seamPairs
    LONG    "V", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  5, 0,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  5, -1     ' FRONT-LEFT (C5 over C1)
    LONG    "V", 2, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    2, 0,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    2, -1     ' TOP-LEFT (C0 beside C1)
    LONG    "V", 3, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   7, 1,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   8, 1      ' LEFT-BOTTOM (C1 beside C2)
    LONG    "V", 4, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 6, 7,  hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 6, 8      ' BOTTOM-RIGHT (C2 beside C3)
    LONG    "V", 5, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 7, 3,  hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 8, 3      ' BOTTOM-BACK (C2 over C4)
seamPairsEnd

DAT ' ---- groups A-F: runs over two and three faces, and full rings ----

' label, number, face, row, column -> face, row, column, panel position, panel row, panel column
runCases
    LONG    "A", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,    3,  7,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  3, 7,  0, 0, 3     ' none
    LONG    "A", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,    3,  8,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  3, 0,  4, 0, 4     ' FRONT.E
    LONG    "A", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,    3, 15,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  3, 7,  4, 7, 4     ' FRONT.E
    LONG    "A", 4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,    3, 16,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   3, 0,  5, 4, 7     ' FRONT.E, RIGHT.E
    LONG    "A", 5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,    3, 20,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   3, 4,  5, 4, 3     ' FRONT.E, RIGHT.E
    LONG    "B", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,    0,  4,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  0, 4,  0, 3, 0     ' none
    LONG    "B", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   -1,  4,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    7, 4,  1, 0, 3     ' FRONT.N
    LONG    "B", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   -8,  4,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    0, 4,  1, 7, 3     ' FRONT.N
    LONG    "B", 4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   -9,  4,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   0, 3,  5, 7, 4     ' FRONT.N, TOP.N
    LONG    "B", 5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -12,  4,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   3, 3,  5, 4, 4     ' FRONT.N, TOP.N
    LONG    "C", 1, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,    -1,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    3, 0,  1, 4, 7     ' LEFT.N
    LONG    "C", 2, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,    -8,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    3, 7,  1, 4, 0     ' LEFT.N
    LONG    "C", 3, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,    -9,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  0, 4,  4, 4, 7     ' LEFT.N, TOP.E
    LONG    "C", 4, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   -10,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  1, 4,  4, 4, 6     ' LEFT.N, TOP.E
    LONG    "D", 1, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,   3,  7,  hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, 3, 7,  3, 3, 7     ' none
    LONG    "D", 2, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,   3,  8,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  7, 3,  4, 3, 0     ' BOTTOM.E
    LONG    "D", 3, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,   3, 15,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  0, 3,  4, 3, 7     ' BOTTOM.E
    LONG    "D", 4, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,   3, 16,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    4, 7,  1, 3, 0     ' BOTTOM.E, RIGHT.N
    LONG    "D", 5, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,   3, 17,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    4, 6,  1, 3, 1     ' BOTTOM.E, RIGHT.N
    LONG    "E", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,    2, 33,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  2, 1,  0, 6, 2     ' four times east: the ring of sides
    LONG    "E", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,    2, -31, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  2, 1,  0, 6, 2     ' four times west: the ring of sides
    LONG    "E", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -30,  5,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  2, 5,  0, 2, 2     ' FRONT.N, TOP.N, BACK.S, BOTTOM.N
    LONG    "F", 1, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,      2, 13,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  5, 5,  4, 5, 2     ' TOP.E
runCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- group K: every corner gap ----

' label, number, face, row, column -> no face, no panel (every coordinate 0)
gapCases
    LONG    "K",  1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -1, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' FRONT-TOP-LEFT
    LONG    "K",  2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -1,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' FRONT-TOP-RIGHT
    LONG    "K",  3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   8,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' FRONT-BOTTOM-RIGHT
    LONG    "K",  4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   8, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' FRONT-BOTTOM-LEFT
    LONG    "K",  5, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   -1, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' BACK-TOP-RIGHT
    LONG    "K",  6, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,   -1,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' BACK-TOP-LEFT
    LONG    "K",  7, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,    8,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' BACK-BOTTOM-LEFT
    LONG    "K",  8, hwEnum.FACE_BACK,    8, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' BACK-BOTTOM-RIGHT
    LONG    "K",  9, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   -1, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' LEFT-TOP-BACK
    LONG    "K", 10, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   -1,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' LEFT-TOP-FRONT
    LONG    "K", 11, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,    8,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' LEFT-BOTTOM-FRONT
    LONG    "K", 12, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,    8, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' LEFT-BOTTOM-BACK
    LONG    "K", 13, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  -1, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' RIGHT-TOP-FRONT
    LONG    "K", 14, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  -1,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' RIGHT-TOP-BACK
    LONG    "K", 15, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,   8,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' RIGHT-BOTTOM-BACK
    LONG    "K", 16, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,   8, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' RIGHT-BOTTOM-FRONT
    LONG    "K", 17, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    -1, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' TOP-BACK-LEFT
    LONG    "K", 18, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    -1,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' TOP-BACK-RIGHT
    LONG    "K", 19, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,     8,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' TOP-FRONT-RIGHT
    LONG    "K", 20, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,     8, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' TOP-FRONT-LEFT
    LONG    "K", 21, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, -1, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' BOTTOM-FRONT-LEFT
    LONG    "K", 22, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM, -1,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' BOTTOM-FRONT-RIGHT
    LONG    "K", 23, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,  8,  8,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' BOTTOM-BACK-RIGHT
    LONG    "K", 24, hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM,  8, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' BOTTOM-BACK-LEFT
    LONG    "K", 25, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, -20, -3,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' deep in the FRONT-TOP-LEFT gap
gapCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- group c, j: a circle of radius 3 centred on the corner pixel FRONT (0,0) ----

' label, number, face, row, column -> face, row, column, panel position, panel row, panel column
' The 16 points of the existing Bresenham circle (drawCircleOfColor) about FRONT (0,0).
circleCases
    LONG    "c",  1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  3,  0,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 3, 0,  0, 7, 3     ' the FRONT arc
    LONG    "c",  2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  0,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 0, 3,  0, 4, 0
    LONG    "c",  3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  3,  1,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 3, 1,  0, 6, 3
    LONG    "c",  4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  1,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 1, 3,  0, 4, 1
    LONG    "c",  5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  2,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 2, 2,  0, 5, 2
    LONG    "c",  6, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, -3,  0,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,   5, 0,  1, 2, 7     ' the TOP arc
    LONG    "c",  7, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, -3,  1,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,   5, 1,  1, 2, 6
    LONG    "c",  8, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, -1,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,   7, 3,  1, 0, 4
    LONG    "c",  9, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, -2,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,   6, 2,  1, 1, 5
    LONG    "c", 10, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  0, -3,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  0, 5,  2, 2, 0     ' the LEFT arc
    LONG    "c", 11, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  3, -1,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  3, 7,  2, 0, 3
    LONG    "c", 12, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  1, -3,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  1, 5,  2, 2, 1
    LONG    "c", 13, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  2, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  2, 6,  2, 1, 2
    LONG    "c", 14, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, -3, -1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0     ' the corner gap
    LONG    "c", 15, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, -1, -3,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0
    LONG    "c", 16, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, -2, -2,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0
' The joins: one step past one arc's end lands exactly on the other arc's end, at each edge.
    LONG    "j",  1, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    8,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 0, 3,  0, 4, 0     ' FRONT-TOP: lands on c2 (TOP (7,3) is c8)
    LONG    "j",  2, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   3,  8,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 3, 0,  0, 7, 3     ' FRONT-LEFT: lands on c1 (LEFT (3,7) is c11)
    LONG    "j",  3, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    5, -1,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  0, 5,  2, 2, 0     ' TOP-LEFT: lands on c10 (TOP (5,0) is c6)
circleCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- group h: an object's home, which places the seam ----

' label, number, face, centre row, centre column -> home face, turn, add row, add column
homeCases
    LONG    "h", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3,  4,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 0,  0,   0     ' on the face
    LONG    "h", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -2,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,   0,  8,   0     ' FRONT.N
    LONG    "h", 3, hwEnum.FACE_TOP,     4, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  3, -1,   0     ' TOP.W
    LONG    "h", 4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3, 18,  hwEnum.FACE_BACK,  0,  0, -16     ' FRONT.E, then RIGHT.E
    LONG    "h", 5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -3, -1,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,   0,  8,   0     ' gap: the column overshoots less, so it is held; FRONT.N
    LONG    "h", 6, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -2, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,   0,  8,   0     ' gap, a tie: the column is held; FRONT.N
    LONG    "h", 7, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -1, -3,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  0,  0,   8     ' gap: the row overshoots less, so it is held; FRONT.W
    LONG    "h", 8, hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  -10,  3,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT, 2, -9,   7     ' LEFT.N, then TOP.E
    LONG    "h", 9, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   0,  0,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 0,  0,   0     ' the corner circle's home
homeCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- groups b, o, s, q, t: face-centric boxes, circles and text ----

' label, number, face, first row, first column, last row, last column, probe row, probe column
'   -> the face that holds the midpoint of the rectangle, and the probe's display row and column
' The midpoint is (first + last) SAR 1; the home transform carries the probe into that face's
' frame, where it folds onto the face that holds it. Panel mapping used below (N = 8, from the
' reference cube): FRONT P0 (7-c, r) +(0,8); TOP P1 (7-r, 7-c) +(8,0); LEFT P2 (7-c, r) +(8,8);
' RIGHT P4 (c, 7-r) +(8,24). Edges used: FRONT.N (r+8, c)  FRONT.E (r, c-8)  FRONT.W (r, c+8)
' LEFT.N (c, -1-r)  LEFT.E (r, c-8)  RIGHT.W (r, c+8)  TOP.S (r-8, c).
extentCases
    ' b1-b4: a box at FRONT (2,5), 6 wide and 4 high, crossing FRONT.E; rows 2..5, columns 5..10,
    '   midpoint (3,7): on FRONT, so home FRONT
    LONG    "b", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   2,  5,  5, 10,   2,  5,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  2, 10     ' FRONT (2,5) -> P0 (2,2)
    LONG    "b", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   2,  5,  5, 10,   2, 10,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 10, 29     ' FRONT.E -> RIGHT (2,2) -> P4 (2,5)
    LONG    "b", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   2,  5,  5, 10,   5, 10,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 10, 26     ' FRONT.E -> RIGHT (5,2) -> P4 (2,2)
    LONG    "b", 4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   2,  5,  5, 10,   5,  8,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  8, 26     ' FRONT.E -> RIGHT (5,0) -> P4 (0,2)
    ' b5-b7: a box at FRONT (-3,2), 5 wide and 5 high, crossing FRONT.N; rows -3..1, columns 2..6,
    '   midpoint (-1,4): past FRONT.N, so home TOP with the transform (r+8, c)
    LONG    "b", 5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -3,  2,  1,  6,  -3,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,   10,  5     ' home (5,2) on TOP -> P1 (2,5)
    LONG    "b", 6, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -3,  2,  1,  6,   1,  6,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    1,  9     ' home (9,6) -> TOP.S -> FRONT (1,6) -> P0 (1,1)
    LONG    "b", 7, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -3,  2,  1,  6,  -1,  4,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    8,  3     ' home (7,4) on TOP -> P1 (0,3)
    ' b8: a box at FRONT (-1,3), 3 wide and 2 high; rows -1..0: the midpoint row is (-1+0) SAR 1 = -1,
    '   which floors (truncating toward zero would give 0, on FRONT): home TOP
    LONG    "b", 8, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  -1,  3,  0,  5,   0,  4,  hwEnum.FACE_TOP,    3,  8     ' home (8,4) -> TOP.S -> FRONT (0,4) -> P0 (3,0)
    ' o1-o5: a circle of radius 4 centred at FRONT (3,6), crossing FRONT.E; the point offsets of
    '   the Bresenham circle are (+-4,0) (0,+-4) (+-4,+-1) (+-1,+-4) (+-3,+-2) (+-2,+-3); home FRONT
    LONG    "o", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3,  6,  3,  6,   3, 10,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 10, 28     ' offset (0,+4): RIGHT (3,2) -> P4 (2,4)
    LONG    "o", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3,  6,  3,  6,   1,  9,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  9, 30     ' offset (-2,+3): RIGHT (1,1) -> P4 (1,6)
    LONG    "o", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3,  6,  3,  6,   3,  2,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  5, 11     ' offset (0,-4): FRONT (3,2) -> P0 (5,3)
    LONG    "o", 4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3,  6,  3,  6,   7,  6,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  1, 15     ' offset (+4,0): FRONT (7,6) -> P0 (1,7)
    LONG    "o", 5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3,  6,  3,  6,   5,  9,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,  9, 26     ' offset (+2,+3): RIGHT (5,1) -> P4 (1,2)
    ' s1-s5: a circle of radius 4 centred at FRONT (3,-2), straddling the FRONT-TOP-LEFT corner off
    '   centre: the centre is past FRONT.W, so home LEFT with the transform (r, c+8), centre LEFT (3,6).
    '   In FRONT's own frame the three points past both edges (-1,-1) (-1,-2) (-1,-3) would be in the
    '   corner gap and lost; homed on LEFT they are on TOP (the seam is on the TOP-FRONT edge, far from the centre)
    LONG    "s", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3, -2,  3, -2,  -1, -1,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   8,  7     ' offset (-4,+1): home (-1,7) -> LEFT.N -> TOP (7,0) -> P1 (0,7)
    LONG    "s", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3, -2,  3, -2,  -1, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   9,  7     ' offset (-4,0): home (-1,6) -> TOP (6,0) -> P1 (1,7)
    LONG    "s", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3, -2,  3, -2,  -1, -3,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  10,  7     ' offset (-4,-1): home (-1,5) -> TOP (5,0) -> P1 (2,7)
    LONG    "s", 4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3, -2,  3, -2,   0,  0,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,   7,  8     ' offset (-3,+2): home (0,8) -> LEFT.E -> FRONT (0,0) -> P0 (7,0)
    LONG    "s", 5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3, -2,  3, -2,   3, -6,  hwEnum.FACE_LEFT,  13, 11     ' offset (0,-4): home (3,2) on LEFT -> P2 (5,3)
    LONG    "s", 6, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   3,  1,  3,  1,  -1, -1,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, cube.NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL, cube.NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL     ' the same pixel with a centre on FRONT: home FRONT, in the corner gap
    ' q1-q6: a circle of radius 4 centred at FRONT (1,1), straddling the corner with its centre on
    '   FRONT: home FRONT, so the seam is on the TOP-LEFT edge, the edge farthest from the centre;
    '   the points past both edges of FRONT (-2,-1) and (-1,-2) are in the gap and not drawn
    LONG    "q", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  1,  1,  1,  -3,  1,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 10,  6     ' offset (-4,0): FRONT.N -> TOP (5,1) -> P1 (2,6)
    LONG    "q", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  1,  1,  1,   1, -3,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 10,  9     ' offset (0,-4): FRONT.W -> LEFT (1,5) -> P2 (2,1)
    LONG    "q", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  1,  1,  1,  -2, -1,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, cube.NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL, cube.NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL     ' offset (-3,-2): the corner gap
    LONG    "q", 4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  1,  1,  1,  -1, -2,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, cube.NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL, cube.NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL     ' offset (-2,-3): the corner gap
    LONG    "q", 5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  1,  1,  1,  -3,  0,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 10,  7     ' offset (-4,-1): FRONT.N -> TOP (5,0) -> P1 (2,7)
    LONG    "q", 6, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  1,  1,  1,   0, -3,  hwEnum.FACE_FRONT, 10,  8     ' offset (-1,-4): FRONT.W -> LEFT (0,5) -> P2 (2,0)
    ' t1-t6: the text "LL" at FRONT (1,5): two 5 x 7 characters one pitch of 6 apart, so rows 1..7 and
    '   columns 5..15 (character 0 at columns 5..9, character 1 at 11..15), crossing FRONT.E;
    '   midpoint (4,10) is past FRONT.E, so home RIGHT with the transform (r, c-8). Each probe is a
    '   lit pixel of an 'L' (its left column, or its bottom row)
    LONG    "t", 1, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  5,  7, 15,   1,  5,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  2,  9     ' character 0, glyph (0,0): home (1,-3) -> RIGHT.W -> FRONT (1,5) -> P0 (2,1)
    LONG    "t", 2, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  5,  7, 15,   4,  5,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  2, 12     ' character 0, glyph (3,0): home (4,-3) -> FRONT (4,5) -> P0 (2,4)
    LONG    "t", 3, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  5,  7, 15,   7,  9,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  9, 24     ' character 0, glyph (6,4): home (7,1) on RIGHT -> P4 (1,0)
    LONG    "t", 4, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  5,  7, 15,   1, 11,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT, 11, 30     ' character 1, glyph (0,0): home (1,3) on RIGHT -> P4 (3,6)
    LONG    "t", 5, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  5,  7, 15,   7, 15,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT, 15, 24     ' character 1, glyph (6,4): home (7,7) on RIGHT -> P4 (7,0)
    LONG    "t", 6, hwEnum.FACE_FRONT,   1,  5,  7, 15,   7,  5,  hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT,  2, 15     ' character 0, glyph (6,0): home (7,-3) -> FRONT (7,5) -> P0 (2,7)
extentCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- group I: faces that are not cube faces ----

' label, number, face, row, column -> no face, no panel (every coordinate 0)
invalidFaceCases
    LONG    "I", 1, hwEnum.FACE_TOP - 1,   1, 1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0
    LONG    "I", 2, hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT + 1, 1, 1,  cube.NO_FACE, 0, 0,  cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION, 0, 0
invalidFaceCasesEnd

DAT ' ---- Test State (singleton) ----

caseCount       LONG    0                                         ' cases run so far
passCount       LONG    0                                         ' cases that passed
failCount       LONG    0                                         ' cases that failed
textLen         LONG    0                                         ' characters written to the line so far
lineText        BYTE    0[LINE_BYTES]                             ' one printed line

PUB main()
'' Fold the reference net, run every case, print one PASS or FAIL line per case, then the
'' total and END_SESSION, then hold.
''

  debug("CUBE FOLD SELF-TEST: reference cube, face size ", udec_(FACE_SIZE), ", folded into chain index ", udec_(TEST_CHAIN))
  caseCount := passCount := failCount := 0

  runNetCases(@netCases, @netCasesEnd)
  runFoldCases(@onFaceCases, @onFaceCasesEnd)
  runFoldCases(@edgeCases, @edgeCasesEnd)
  runPairCases(@seamPairs, @seamPairsEnd)
  runFoldCases(@runCases, @runCasesEnd)
  runFoldCases(@gapCases, @gapCasesEnd)
  runFoldCases(@circleCases, @circleCasesEnd)
  runHomeCases(@homeCases, @homeCasesEnd)
  runExtentCases(@extentCases, @extentCasesEnd)
  runFoldCases(@invalidFaceCases, @invalidFaceCasesEnd)

  debug("CUBE FOLD SELF-TEST: ", udec_(caseCount), " cases, ", udec_(passCount), " PASS, ", udec_(failCount), " FAIL")
  debug("END_SESSION")

  repeat                                                        ' hold

PRI runNetCases(pFirst, pEnd) | pCase, mistakeCount, bPass
' Fold each net of group N and compare the problems foldNet() reports with the expected count.
'
' @param pFirst - address of the first net case
' @param pEnd - address just past the last net case

' Local Variables:
' @local pCase - address of the case being run
' @local mistakeCount - problems foldNet() reported
' @local bPass - TRUE when the case passed

  pCase := pFirst
  repeat while pCase < pEnd
    mistakeCount := cube.foldNet(TEST_CHAIN, @LONG[pCase][NET_ROWS], @LONG[pCase][NET_COLUMNS], @refCablePositions, LONG[pCase][NET_TOP], LONG[pCase][NET_FRONT], FACE_SIZE)
    bPass := mistakeCount == LONG[pCase][NET_EXPECTED]
    startLine(bPass, LONG[pCase][NET_LABEL], LONG[pCase][NET_NUMBER])
    addText(@"top C")
    addNumber(LONG[pCase][NET_TOP])
    addText(@", front C")
    addNumber(LONG[pCase][NET_FRONT])
    addText(@" -> ")
    addNumber(mistakeCount)
    addText(@" problem(s)")
    if bPass == FALSE
      addText(@" expected ")
      addNumber(LONG[pCase][NET_EXPECTED])
    finishLine(bPass)
    pCase += NET_CASE_LONGS * hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG

PRI runFoldCases(pFirst, pEnd) | pCase, eFace, faceRow, faceColumn, panelPosn, panelRow, panelColumn, displayRow, displayColumn, expDisplayRow, expDisplayColumn, bPass
' Push each case's face coordinates through the fold and compare where they land (face, face
' coordinates, panel position, panel coordinates, display coordinates) with the hand answer.
'
' @param pFirst - address of the first fold case
' @param pEnd - address just past the last fold case

' Local Variables:
' @local pCase - address of the case being run
' @local eFace - the face the pixel landed on
' @local faceRow - the pixel's row on that face
' @local faceColumn - the pixel's column on that face
' @local panelPosn - the panel position (P0 .. P5), or NO_PANEL_POSITION
' @local panelRow - the pixel's row on that panel
' @local panelColumn - the pixel's column on that panel
' @local displayRow - the display row the pixel landed on
' @local displayColumn - the display column the pixel landed on
' @local expDisplayRow - the expected display row (from the hand table of panel origins)
' @local expDisplayColumn - the expected display column
' @local bPass - TRUE when the case passed

  pCase := pFirst
  repeat while pCase < pEnd
    eFace, faceRow, faceColumn := cube.foldFacePixel(TEST_CHAIN, LONG[pCase][FOLD_FACE], LONG[pCase][FOLD_ROW], LONG[pCase][FOLD_COL])
    panelPosn, panelRow, panelColumn, displayRow, displayColumn := cube.facePixelToPanel(TEST_CHAIN, LONG[pCase][FOLD_FACE], LONG[pCase][FOLD_ROW], LONG[pCase][FOLD_COL])
    expDisplayRow, expDisplayColumn := expectedDisplay(LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL], LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL_ROW], LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL_COL])
    bPass := (eFace == LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_FACE]) and (faceRow == LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_ROW]) and (faceColumn == LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_COL])
    bPass := bPass and (panelPosn == LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL]) and (panelRow == LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL_ROW]) and (panelColumn == LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL_COL])
    bPass := bPass and (displayRow == expDisplayRow) and (displayColumn == expDisplayColumn)
    startLine(bPass, LONG[pCase][FOLD_LABEL], LONG[pCase][FOLD_NUMBER])
    addFaceAt(LONG[pCase][FOLD_FACE], LONG[pCase][FOLD_ROW], LONG[pCase][FOLD_COL])
    addText(@" -> ")
    addLanding(eFace, faceRow, faceColumn, panelPosn, panelRow, panelColumn, displayRow, displayColumn)
    if bPass == FALSE
      addText(@" expected ")
      addLanding(LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_FACE], LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_ROW], LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_COL], LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL], LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL_ROW], LONG[pCase][FOLD_EXP_PANEL_COL], expDisplayRow, expDisplayColumn)
    finishLine(bPass)
    pCase += FOLD_CASE_LONGS * hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG

PRI runPairCases(pFirst, pEnd) | pCase, panelA, rowA, columnA, panelB, rowB, columnB, bPass
' For each edge the flat picture shows, check that the last pixel on a face and the first one
' past its edge are neighbours on the display. This checks the up conventions against the
' wiring itself, independently of any hand-computed value.
'
' @param pFirst - address of the first seam pair
' @param pEnd - address just past the last seam pair

' Local Variables:
' @local pCase - address of the case being run
' @local panelA - panel position the last pixel on the face lands on
' @local rowA - its display row
' @local columnA - its display column
' @local panelB - panel position the first pixel past the edge lands on
' @local rowB - its display row
' @local columnB - its display column
' @local bPass - TRUE when the case passed

  pCase := pFirst
  repeat while pCase < pEnd
    panelA, _, _, rowA, columnA := cube.facePixelToPanel(TEST_CHAIN, LONG[pCase][PAIR_FACE_A], LONG[pCase][PAIR_ROW_A], LONG[pCase][PAIR_COL_A])
    panelB, _, _, rowB, columnB := cube.facePixelToPanel(TEST_CHAIN, LONG[pCase][PAIR_FACE_B], LONG[pCase][PAIR_ROW_B], LONG[pCase][PAIR_COL_B])
    bPass := (panelA <> cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION) and (panelB <> cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION)
    bPass := bPass and (abs(rowA - rowB) + abs(columnA - columnB) == DISPLAY_NEIGHBOURS)
    startLine(bPass, LONG[pCase][PAIR_LABEL], LONG[pCase][PAIR_NUMBER])
    addFaceAt(LONG[pCase][PAIR_FACE_A], LONG[pCase][PAIR_ROW_A], LONG[pCase][PAIR_COL_A])
    addText(@" d")
    addPoint(rowA, columnA)
    addText(@" | ")
    addFaceAt(LONG[pCase][PAIR_FACE_B], LONG[pCase][PAIR_ROW_B], LONG[pCase][PAIR_COL_B])
    addText(@" d")
    addPoint(rowB, columnB)
    if bPass == TRUE
      addText(@": display neighbours")
    else
      addText(@": NOT display neighbours")
    finishLine(bPass)
    pCase += PAIR_CASE_LONGS * hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG

PRI runHomeCases(pFirst, pEnd) | pCase, eHomeFace, homeTurn, homeAddRow, homeAddColumn, bPass
' Find each object centre's home and compare the home face and transform with the hand answer.
'
' @param pFirst - address of the first home case
' @param pEnd - address just past the last home case

' Local Variables:
' @local pCase - address of the case being run
' @local eHomeFace - the face the object is homed on
' @local homeTurn - quarter turns into the home frame
' @local homeAddRow - row added after the turn
' @local homeAddColumn - column added after the turn
' @local bPass - TRUE when the case passed

  pCase := pFirst
  repeat while pCase < pEnd
    eHomeFace, homeTurn, homeAddRow, homeAddColumn := cube.homeOnFace(TEST_CHAIN, LONG[pCase][HOME_FACE], LONG[pCase][HOME_ROW], LONG[pCase][HOME_COL])
    bPass := (eHomeFace == LONG[pCase][HOME_EXP_FACE]) and (homeTurn == LONG[pCase][HOME_EXP_TURN])
    bPass := bPass and (homeAddRow == LONG[pCase][HOME_EXP_ADD_ROW]) and (homeAddColumn == LONG[pCase][HOME_EXP_ADD_COL])
    startLine(bPass, LONG[pCase][HOME_LABEL], LONG[pCase][HOME_NUMBER])
    addFaceAt(LONG[pCase][HOME_FACE], LONG[pCase][HOME_ROW], LONG[pCase][HOME_COL])
    addText(@" -> ")
    addHome(eHomeFace, homeTurn, homeAddRow, homeAddColumn)
    if bPass == FALSE
      addText(@" expected ")
      addHome(LONG[pCase][HOME_EXP_FACE], LONG[pCase][HOME_EXP_TURN], LONG[pCase][HOME_EXP_ADD_ROW], LONG[pCase][HOME_EXP_ADD_COL])
    finishLine(bPass)
    pCase += HOME_CASE_LONGS * hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG

PRI runExtentCases(pFirst, pEnd) | pCase, eHomeFace, homeTurn, homeAddRow, homeAddColumn, displayRow, displayColumn, bPass
' For each probe pixel of a face-centric object, do what the display does to draw it: home the
' object on the face that holds the midpoint of the rectangle it spans, then carry the probe into
' that frame and fold it onto the face that holds it, and compare the home face and the display
' pixel with the hand answer. A wrong midpoint (truncating instead of flooring), a wrong home
' transform, a seam on the wrong edge or a wrong fold changes the home face or the pixel.
'
' @param pFirst - address of the first extent case
' @param pEnd - address just past the last extent case

' Local Variables:
' @local pCase - address of the case being run
' @local eHomeFace - the face the object is homed on
' @local homeTurn - quarter turns into the home frame
' @local homeAddRow - row added after the turn
' @local homeAddColumn - column added after the turn
' @local displayRow - the display row the probe landed on
' @local displayColumn - the display column the probe landed on
' @local bPass - TRUE when the case passed

  pCase := pFirst
  repeat while pCase < pEnd
    eHomeFace, homeTurn, homeAddRow, homeAddColumn := cube.homeOnFaceOfExtent(TEST_CHAIN, LONG[pCase][EXT_FACE], LONG[pCase][EXT_FIRST_ROW], LONG[pCase][EXT_FIRST_COL], LONG[pCase][EXT_LAST_ROW], LONG[pCase][EXT_LAST_COL])
    displayRow, displayColumn := cube.homeFoldToDisplay(TEST_CHAIN, eHomeFace, homeTurn, homeAddRow, homeAddColumn, LONG[pCase][EXT_PROBE_ROW], LONG[pCase][EXT_PROBE_COL])
    bPass := (eHomeFace == LONG[pCase][EXT_EXP_HOME]) and (displayRow == LONG[pCase][EXT_EXP_ROW]) and (displayColumn == LONG[pCase][EXT_EXP_COL])
    startLine(bPass, LONG[pCase][EXT_LABEL], LONG[pCase][EXT_NUMBER])
    addFaceAt(LONG[pCase][EXT_FACE], LONG[pCase][EXT_PROBE_ROW], LONG[pCase][EXT_PROBE_COL])
    addText(@" of ")
    addPoint(LONG[pCase][EXT_FIRST_ROW], LONG[pCase][EXT_FIRST_COL])
    addText(@"-")
    addPoint(LONG[pCase][EXT_LAST_ROW], LONG[pCase][EXT_LAST_COL])
    addText(@" -> ")
    addExtentLanding(eHomeFace, displayRow, displayColumn)
    if bPass == FALSE
      addText(@" expected ")
      addExtentLanding(LONG[pCase][EXT_EXP_HOME], LONG[pCase][EXT_EXP_ROW], LONG[pCase][EXT_EXP_COL])
    finishLine(bPass)
    pCase += EXT_CASE_LONGS * hwEnum.BYTES_PER_LONG

PRI expectedDisplay(panelPosn, panelRow, panelColumn) : displayRow, displayColumn
' Return the display coordinates of panel coordinates, from the hand table of panel origins.
'
' @param panelPosn - the panel position (P0 .. P5), or NO_PANEL_POSITION
' @param panelRow - row on that panel
' @param panelColumn - column on that panel
' @returns displayRow - display row, or 0 when there is no panel
' @returns displayColumn - display column, or 0 when there is no panel

  displayRow := displayColumn := 0
  if panelPosn <> cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION
    displayRow := panelRow + panelOriginRows[panelPosn]
    displayColumn := panelColumn + panelOriginColumns[panelPosn]

PRI startLine(bPass, labelChar, labelNumber)
' Start one result line: PASS or FAIL, the case number, and the case's label.
'
' @param bPass - TRUE when the case passed
' @param labelChar - the label's letter
' @param labelNumber - the label's number

  caseCount++
  textLen := 0
  if bPass == TRUE
    addText(@"PASS ")
  else
    addText(@"FAIL ")
  addNumber(caseCount)
  addText(@" ")
  lineText[textLen++] := labelChar
  addNumber(labelNumber)
  addText(@": ")

PRI finishLine(bPass)
' Print the result line and count the case.
'
' @param bPass - TRUE when the case passed

  lineText[textLen] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineText))
  if bPass == TRUE
    passCount++
  else
    failCount++

PRI addLanding(eFace, faceRow, faceColumn, panelPosn, panelRow, panelColumn, displayRow, displayColumn)
' Append where a pixel landed: "TOP (6,3) P1 (1,4) d(9,4)".
'
' @param eFace - the face (hwEnum.FACE_*), or NO_FACE
' @param faceRow - row on that face
' @param faceColumn - column on that face
' @param panelPosn - the panel position (P0 .. P5), or NO_PANEL_POSITION
' @param panelRow - row on that panel
' @param panelColumn - column on that panel
' @param displayRow - display row, or NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL
' @param displayColumn - display column, or NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL

  addFaceAt(eFace, faceRow, faceColumn)
  addText(@" P")
  if panelPosn == cube.NO_PANEL_POSITION
    addText(@"-")
  else
    addNumber(panelPosn)
  addText(@" ")
  addPoint(panelRow, panelColumn)
  addText(@" d")
  addPoint(displayRow, displayColumn)

PRI addExtentLanding(eHomeFace, displayRow, displayColumn)
' Append where an object's probe landed: "TOP d(10,5)".
'
' @param eHomeFace - the face the object is homed on (hwEnum.FACE_*), or NO_FACE
' @param displayRow - display row, or NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL
' @param displayColumn - display column, or NO_DISPLAY_PIXEL

  addText(faceText(eHomeFace))
  addText(@" d")
  addPoint(displayRow, displayColumn)

PRI addHome(eHomeFace, homeTurn, homeAddRow, homeAddColumn)
' Append an object's home: "TOP turn 0 add (8,0)".
'
' @param eHomeFace - the face the object is homed on (hwEnum.FACE_*), or NO_FACE
' @param homeTurn - quarter turns into the home frame
' @param homeAddRow - row added after the turn
' @param homeAddColumn - column added after the turn

  addText(faceText(eHomeFace))
  addText(@" turn ")
  addNumber(homeTurn)
  addText(@" add ")
  addPoint(homeAddRow, homeAddColumn)

PRI addFaceAt(eFace, row, column)
' Append a face and coordinates on it: "FRONT (-2,3)".
'
' @param eFace - the face (hwEnum.FACE_*), or NO_FACE
' @param row - row on that face
' @param column - column on that face

  addText(faceText(eFace))
  addText(@" ")
  addPoint(row, column)

PRI addPoint(row, column)
' Append coordinates: "(row,column)".
'
' @param row - the row
' @param column - the column

  addText(@"(")
  addNumber(row)
  addText(@",")
  addNumber(column)
  addText(@")")

PRI addText(pText)
' Append a zero-terminated string to the line.
'
' @param pText - pointer to the zero-terminated string

  repeat while BYTE[pText] <> 0
    lineText[textLen++] := BYTE[pText++]

PRI addNumber(number) | divisor
' Append a signed decimal number to the line.
'
' @param number - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the place value of the digit being written

  if number < 0
    lineText[textLen++] := "-"
    number := -number
  divisor := ONES_PLACE
  repeat while number / divisor >= cube.DECIMAL_BASE
    divisor *= cube.DECIMAL_BASE
  repeat while divisor >= ONES_PLACE
    lineText[textLen++] := "0" + (number / divisor) // cube.DECIMAL_BASE
    divisor /= cube.DECIMAL_BASE

PRI faceText(eFace) : pName
' Return the name of a face.
'
' @param eFace - the face (hwEnum.FACE_*), NO_FACE, or any other value
' @returns pName - pointer to the zero-terminated name

  case eFace
    hwEnum.FACE_TOP:
      pName := @"TOP"
    hwEnum.FACE_BOTTOM:
      pName := @"BOTTOM"
    hwEnum.FACE_FRONT:
      pName := @"FRONT"
    hwEnum.FACE_BACK:
      pName := @"BACK"
    hwEnum.FACE_LEFT:
      pName := @"LEFT"
    hwEnum.FACE_RIGHT:
      pName := @"RIGHT"
    cube.NO_FACE:
      pName := @"NO_FACE"
    other:
      pName := @"NOT_A_FACE"

